\f1\fs22 \'93Not all of the accounts. There exists off-shore accounts, vast sums in various tax havens, that cannot be accessed by anyone other than Jamison Hardy or his heir. The next closest relative is determined by examination of the applicants DNA, not fancy documentation and no-one, to this day, has managed to lay claim to the money and live long enough to spend it. On each and every occasion the banks have been approached by a claimant, they are at once cut down by a coparcener or the enemies of Jamison Hardy. The wealthiest in the world have hatched schemes for decades trying to access the money hidden away, but they have always failed. There are trillions waiting to be liberated and this lump of human refuse sitting here before you is the only person in the world who can access the accounts.\'94\
\'93Who do you think the target was for the Stick-it-Inn bombing?\'94\
\'93Me?\'94 Chanta was still in denial. \'93Am I so important that hundreds of other are killed just to get to me? No, it is not possible.\'94\
\'93How many heirs were under protection?\'94 The number of relatives of Jamison Hardy must run into the hundreds, she thought.\
\'93I don\'92t know exactly. There were numerous cells that operate independently, but have diminished over the years as each heir was murdered. Jamison was perfectly aware his progeny were under threat and even while he was still alive, plots were being hatched and alliances forged. All for the one purpose of wrestling away his hidden wealth. Publicly acknowledging any of his numerous descendants would have placed them in mortal danger. He concluded it was safer to leave them to their own devices, offering up no overt assistance, just covert protection teams.\'94\
\'93No, I was never your friend.\'94 Haloren replied with no shame. He had a job to do and emotional attachments would prove counter-productive. \
\'93You have been under observation and our protection for most of your life. The only reason you are still alive is because of me and my company of dedicated defenders.\'94\
\'93Bullshit.\'94 Chanta found it hard to believe that his shit-filled existence was, in reality, charmed and he had reason to be grateful. By any objective measure his life had been one of hardship and deprivation and he firmly believed he had solid grounds for complaint. \
 \'93Who do you think brought you up?\'94 Halo looked Chanta up and down and then smiled at Detective Lanning.\
\'93My uncle, Chester. At least that\'92s what he told me.\'94\
\'93Indeed, that is what he told you. He was not your uncle, but one of the first to join the team.\'94\
\'93But he abandoned me when I was 16 years old. Fucking prick went out one day and never came back.\'94\
\'93That fucking prick, as you call him, was tortured and killed that day and the fact that you are still alive means he kept his mouth shut. You have much to be grateful for.\'94\
\'93I didn\'92t know that and could not know that, but I was left high and dry while not yet a man. I didn\'92t know when I was to be kicked out onto the street and have spent all the years since frightened at the prospect of being homeless. I have never paid rent, I don\'92t know where or who to pay. You are level 6 and could never imagine the creeping sickness of that constant, unrelenting anxiety, not knowing what would happen from to me one day to the next.\'94\
\'93No one knows that, you idiot. There is no such thing as certainty, just the promise of it. Don\'92t you know that?\'94 The great teacher needed an education. \'93You lazy minded, useless level 2 turd. Have you ever bothered to read the documents Chester left for you. They were sent shortly after of he died. Did you read them?\'94\
\'93No. I couldn\'92t be bothered. As far as I was concerned he abandoned me and I wasn\'92t interested in anything he had to say. (????) He could go fuck himself.\'94\
\'93Idiot. You own the apartment. I could never understand why you didn\'92t sell up and improve your station. I guess being a complete moron slowed you down.\'94 Haloren was incensed. 
\f2\i I have been protecting this imbecile for years. What a fucking waste of time, unless of course I can get hold of some of that cash. The ultimate prize.
